  "e2-s16": { name: "A parcel pushed along a floor", label: "Graph", intro: R`A $3.0$ kg parcel starts from rest at $x = 0$ on a level, frictionless floor. A horizontal force pushes the parcel along the $x$-axis. The graph shows the $x$-component of the force as a function of the parcel's position.`, sources: one([{ svg: parcelFx() }]) },
  "e2-s18": { name: "Soap on a tray", label: "Bar chart", intro: R`A bar of soap slides down a rough, tilted tray from point 1 to point 2. The bar chart shows the soap's kinetic energy and gravitational potential energy, and the thermal energy of the soap and tray, at each point. The soap and tray exchange no energy with their surroundings. The thermal energy at point 2 is not shown.`, sources: one([{ svg: soapBars() }]) },
  "e2-s19": { name: "A parcel, a rough floor, and a spring", label: "Diagram", intro: R`A parcel of mass $m$ is released from rest at height $h$ on a smooth curved chute. At the bottom, it slides across a horizontal rough section of length $L$, where the coefficient of kinetic friction is $\mu$. It then slides over a smooth section and compresses a spring of spring constant $k$ that is attached to a wall, as shown. The parcel reaches the spring, so $h > \mu L$.`, sources: one([{ svg: chuteDiagram() }]) },
  "e2-s21": { name: "Work done by a scooter motor", label: "Graph", intro: R`The motor of an electric scooter exerts a constant forward force of $8.0$ N on the scooter, along its line of motion. The graph shows the total work $W$ done by the motor as a function of time.`, sources: one([{ svg: scooterW() }]) },
