  "e2-s27": { name: "A lazy Susan slowing down", label: "Graph", intro: R`A lazy Susan, a flat tray that rotates on a table, is spun by hand and then released. The graph shows its angular speed as a function of time. The lazy Susan has a rotational inertia of $0.40$ kg·m² about its axis.`, sources: one([{ svg: lazyW() }]) },
  "e2-s29": { name: "A ratchet", label: "Diagram", intro: R`A mechanic tightens a bolt with a ratchet. The mechanic pushes with a force of magnitude $60$ N at a point on the handle $0.25$ m from the bolt's axis. The force makes an angle of $40^\circ$ with the handle and lies in the plane of rotation, as shown from above.`, sources: one([{ svg: ratchetDiagram() }]) },
